1. PARTIES, ACCEPTANCE AND SCOPE
This Agreement governs the AresEdge SDK, its compiled libraries, public wrappers,
models, documentation, examples and updates (Software). "Licensor" is the legal
entity trading as Ares Defence Labs identified on the applicable purchase order,
invoice or portal checkout (Order). "Licensee" is the person or entity accepting
these terms. By installing, copying or using the Software, Licensee accepts this
Agreement. A person accepting for an entity represents that they can bind it.
If Licensee does not accept, it must not use or distribute the Software.
An Order accepted by Licensor may specify application identifiers, platforms,
products, fees, term, permitted developers and additional rights. A conflicting
express provision of that Order controls; otherwise this Agreement applies.

2. COMMERCIAL GRANT
Subject to payment, the Order and compliance with this Agreement, Licensor grants
Licensee a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence during the authorised
term to install and use the Software for developing, testing and maintaining the
applications specified in the Order, and to distribute the Software solely in
compiled form as an integral part of those applications to their end users.
End users may run the incorporated Software only as part of the authorised app
and only while the applicable entitlement permits. No independent SDK licence
or sublicensing right is granted to end users. Contractors may use the Software
solely for Licensee's authorised work and under equivalent confidentiality and
use restrictions; Licensee remains responsible for their compliance. Affiliates,
additional apps and additional products require express coverage in the Order.
No ownership, exclusivity or source-code delivery is granted.

3. EVALUATION
Without a paid entitlement, the Software may be used solely for internal technical
evaluation under its trial restrictions, including the shared 60-second process
trial. Restarting an evaluation application does not authorise production use.
Trial access is not a perpetual, free, production or redistribution licence.
Licensor may offer different evaluation rights in writing. Trial notices and
technical limits must not be removed or bypassed. Evaluation ends when withdrawn
by Licensor, superseded by an Order, or terminated under this Agreement.

4. TERM, KEYS AND RENEWAL
Unless an Order states otherwise, paid customer entitlements last twelve months
from their signed term start and end on their signed expiry date. Offline
verification does not extend the term. Licence keys are specific to permitted
applications, platforms and products. They must not be shared outside authorised
development and distribution of those applications. Licensor alone issues keys.
Renewal, automatic billing, amounts, taxes, cancellation and refunds are governed
by the accepted Order and checkout terms, subject to mandatory law. Where renewal
is arranged approximately thirty days before expiry, Licensee must incorporate
the replacement key and distribute updated applications before the old key
expires. Existing app installations containing an expired key may enter trial
or lose protected functionality. There is no implied grace period after expiry
and no guarantee that an already distributed app can operate perpetually.
Non-expiring owner entitlements, if expressly issued, are limited to their signed
scope and do not grant general customer, resale or transfer rights.

5. RESTRICTIONS
Except as expressly permitted by this Agreement or non-excludable law, Licensee
must not: (a) resell, sublicense, rent, lend or distribute the Software as an SDK,
standalone library, development service or competing reusable component;
(b) distribute implementation source, SDK binaries or models separately from an
authorised compiled application; (c) extract or use models outside the authorised
SDK integration, or use them to train another model; (d) reverse engineer,
decompile, disassemble or attempt to derive proprietary source or model internals;
(e) forge, alter, share or circumvent keys, signatures, trial controls, identity
checks or other licensing mechanisms; (f) remove proprietary or third-party
notices; (g) use the Software unlawfully or infringe third-party rights; or
(h) represent that Licensor endorses Licensee's application without permission.
These restrictions do not prohibit activities that applicable law expressly
permits despite contractual restrictions. Public APIs may be used as documented.

6. DOCUMENTATION, WRAPPERS AND EXAMPLES
